.Dd August 3, 2026
.Dt XPT 8
.Os

.Sh NAME

.Nm xpt
.Nd package manager utility

.Sh SYNOPSIS

.Nm
.Fl V | Fl i | Fl g | Fl h | Fl r | Fl l | Fl t | Fl s | Fl I | Fl B | Fl Q
.Op Fl f Ar file | Fl p Ar package | Fl n Ar net-package
.Op Fl q
.Op Fl d Ar dir

.Sh DESCRIPTION

.Nm
is a package management utility designed to install, remove and administer
.Pa .xpt
packages.
it is designed as both a high-level and a medium-level interface for package management.

.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds

.It Fl V
show the current
.Nm
version.

.It Fl i
install a package, specified by one of the package reference flags.

.It Fl g
get the version of an installed package.

.It Fl h
show the help message.

.It Fl r
remove an installed package.

.It Fl l
list the installed packages.

.It Fl t
show the files used by a package.

.It Fl s
download the repository indexes.

.It Fl I
show information about an installed package

.It Fl B
print the libxpt build info

.It Fl Q
get information about a package from a repository.

.El

.Sh OPTIONS

.Bl -tag -width Ds

.It Fl f
specify a
.Pa .xpt
package file.

.It Fl p
specify an installed package name.

.It Fl d
specify a destination directory for the operations.

.It Fl n
specify a package from one of the repositories.

.It Fl q
make the output of most operations quiet (doesn't hide errors).

.El

